  "question": {
    "text": "Glycerine is filled in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>mm</mi></math> wide space between two large plane horizontal surfaces. A thin plate of area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.75</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>mm</mi></math> from one of the surfaces is in a horizontal position between the plates inside the glycerine. It is dragged horizontally at a constant speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.5</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> Take coefficient of viscosity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. What is the force required to drag the plate at a constant speed (in newton)?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-08-21_at_3.50.52_PM.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 130px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "31.25",
